    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1162">

                <pb facs="1050" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/212</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-08T19:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your August 7, 9 a.m. You may inform the Minister for Foreign Affairs that at the
                    request of the Austrian Government the Government <pb facs="1051" n="737"
                        xml:id="pg737"/> of the United States consented to take over Austrian
                    affairs in Russia, and you may inquire whether in these circumstances there
                    would be any objection to temporarily raising the American flag over the
                    Austrian Embassy. Your action in this matter should be guided by the decision of
                    the Foreign Office. Cable result.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
